<section id="A11" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix K </span>Hyperparameters and Configuration for GRPO</h2>

<div id="A11.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present the configuration details of the GRPO-based RL training. The training was conducted on a single node equipped with eight NVIDIA H100 GPUs using the Verl framework.
We initialized the policy from the SFT-trained model checkpoint.
To optimize resource utilization and training efficiency, we enabled Gradient Checkpointing (<span id="A11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">enable_gradient_checkpointing</span>=True) and configured FSDP with both parameter and optimizer offloading (<span id="A11.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">param_offload</span>=True, <span id="A11.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">optimizer_offload</span>=True).</p>
</div>
<div id="A11.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For data and batch settings, the total training batch size (<span id="A11.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">train_batch_size</span>) was set to <math id="A11.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>256</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256</annotation></semantics></math>, with maximum prompt and response lengths capped at <math id="A11.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>15,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15,000</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A11.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10,000</annotation></semantics></math> tokens, respectively. The Actor policy optimization used a learning rate of <math id="A11.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\times 10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times 10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math> and was updated for <math id="A11.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ppo\_epochs=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ppo\_epochs=2</annotation></semantics></math> internal epochs per rollout collection. We disabled the KL loss term and set the gradient clip to <math id="A11.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A11.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The Rollout phase is crucial for model exploration. Rollouts were executed using the vllm engine with a configuration of <math id="A11.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=6</annotation></semantics></math> samples per prompt (<span id="A11.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">rollout.n</span>), a sampling temperature of <math id="A11.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A11.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="top\_p=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">top\_p=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> to encourage diversity. The reward signal was sourced from the external script, and KL-based regularization was explicitly disabled. Furthermore, an overlong buffer penalty was enabled, penalizing responses exceeding <math id="A11.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3,000</annotation></semantics></math> tokens. The entire training process ran for <math id="A11.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math> total epochs. Notably, achieving optimal performance on the WebQSP dataset required only <math id="A11.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="36" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>36</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">36</annotation></semantics></math> steps and <math id="A11.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="119.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>119.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">119.2</annotation></semantics></math> GPU hours, demonstrating the high efficiency of our framework. By detailing the parameter settings of the GRPO phase, we ensured the reproducibility of our <span id="A11.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">EoG</span> model.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A11.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 9: </span>Detailed configuration of training and testing parameters for the GRPO phase.</figcaption>
<table id="A11.T9.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A11.T9.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A11.T9.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><span id="A11.T9.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Category</span></th>
<th id="A11.T9.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">Configuration</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A11.T9.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A11.T9.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><span id="A11.T9.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hardware</span></td>
<td id="A11.T9.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">Compute Hardware: 8 <math id="A11.T9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> H100 GPUs</td></tr>
<tr id="A11.T9.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A11.T9.2.3.1" class="ltx_td" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"></td>
<td id="A11.T9.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">GPU Memory Utilization: 0.6</td></tr>
<tr id="A11.T9.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A11.T9.2.4.1" class="ltx_td" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"></td>
<td id="A11.T9.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">FSDP Offload: Param &amp; Optimizer</td></tr>
<tr id="A11.T9.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
