</figure>
<div id="A14.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A14.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Beyond reporting mean performance scores, we further validated the reliability of our results through statistical hypothesis testing. Table <a href="#A14.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ Appendix N Statistical Evaluation Details ‣ Explore-on-Graph: Incentivizing Autonomous Exploration of Large Language Models on Knowledge Graphs with Path-refined Reward Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> details the t-statistics and p-values comparing EoG with the GCR baseline. In all datasets, We performed a standard t-test, yielding a p-value <math id="A14.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math> 0.05, which confirms that the performance gains of EoG over GCR are statistically significant and not due to random variance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A14.T13" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 13: </span>Statistical comparison between GCR and our EoG framework using a one-sample t-test (<math id="A14.T13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="df=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">df=4</annotation></semantics></math>). The table reports the baseline score, our model’s performance (Mean <math id="A14.T13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> SD), and the calculated <math id="A14.T13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-statistics and <math id="A14.T13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-values. Results indicate statistically significant improvements across all metrics.</figcaption>
